question:
What problem do message queues solve in microservices?
```javascript
// Service A publishes event
queue.publish('user:created', {id: 1, email: 'test@example.com'});
// Service B subscribes
queue.subscribe('user:created', (msg) => {
  sendWelcomeEmail(msg.email);
});
```

What is the difference between synchronous and asynchronous microservice calls?
```javascript
// Sync: wait for response
const user = await userService.getUser(1);

// Async: fire and forget or callback
userService.emitUserFetch(1, callback);
```

What is service discovery?
```javascript
// Services register their location
registry.register('user-service', 'http://user-service-1:3001');
// Client queries registry instead of hardcoding URLs
const url = registry.lookup('user-service');
```

How should microservices handle distributed transactions?
```javascript
// Service A: deduct from account
await accountService.deduct(1, 100);
// Service B: credit to account
await accountService.credit(2, 100);
// What if B fails after A succeeds?
```

What is circuit breaker pattern?
```javascript
// Calls to failing service
if (circuitBreaker.isOpen()) {
  // fail fast without calling service
  throw new Error('Service unavailable');
}
const result = await callService();
```

How should services communicate across networks?
```javascript
// Option A: REST HTTP
fetch('http://service:3001/api/users/1');

// Option B: gRPC (protobuf)
await client.getUser({id: 1});

// Option C: Message Queue
queue.publish('get-user', {id: 1});
```

What challenges arise when logging across microservices?
```javascript
// Service A logs: 'Processing request'
// Service B logs: 'Sending email'
// How do we correlate these as one request?
```

What is the bulkhead pattern?
```javascript
// Dedicate separate thread pools for different services
const userPool = new ThreadPool(10);
const paymentPool = new ThreadPool(5);
// Slow payment service doesn't starve user service
```

